---
description: Job search check-in: what needs {first_name} today, new matches, and the application pipeline
---

You are helping {first_name} with their job search. Hal Employment is a command line in
`{code_dir}` (run commands from there with `python3 -m jobhunt ...`).

1. Run `python3 -m jobhunt mail -q` to pull in new recruiting email, then
   `python3 -m jobhunt inbox -n 15`, `python3 -m jobhunt todo`, `python3 -m jobhunt queue`
   and `python3 -m jobhunt stats`.
2. Read the Pipeline note: `{vault_note}`.
3. Report, briefly and in this order:
   - **Needs you**: assessments, interviews, offers, emails from real people, follow-ups due. For each, say what to do and by when.
   - **Changes** since yesterday (new rejections, confirmations).
   - **Today's shortlist**: from `python3 -m jobhunt list -m 60 -n 15`, pick up to 10 worth applying to today and say why in one line each, following the goal set in Hal Employment.
4. Ask which to shortlist. For each one picked, run `python3 -m jobhunt set <id> shortlisted`;
   Hal Employment prepares their documents and puts them at the front of the queue.
5. Remind {first_name} that applications are made in Hal Employment, opened with `python3 -m jobhunt open`
   (queue, documents, form filling and to-dos).

Rules: never submit an application or send an email on their behalf: draft, and they send.
Status changes go through `python3 -m jobhunt set <id> <status> [note]`.
$ARGUMENTS
